Find out how developers including Insomniac Games and Remedy benefit from the upscaling tech.
QSSR arrives in Marvel’s Spider-Man 2, Control Resonant, The Finals, Arc Raiders, No Man&#8217;s Sky, and Hell Let Loose: Vietnam
Control Resonant featuring QSSR upscaling &nbsp;
Remedy Entertainment is bringing QSSR to Control Resonant on PS5, with noticeable improvements in image stability and fine detail.&nbsp;
&#8220;It&#8217;s great to see PlayStation bringing the same kind of leap on the PS5 that PSSR brought to PS5 Pro. QSSR gives Control Resonant a much more stable and detailed image, and we&#8217;ve worked closely with Sony to have it ready in an update coming in December.&#8221;&nbsp;
Six years after launch, PlayStation 5 is still getting better. Last month, we introduced Quick Spectral Super Resolution (QSSR), bringing AI-guided upscaling to the console you already own. Since then, there&#8217;s been a lot of interest from developers eager to try it out. We&#8217;re happy to announce that the next set of games is on the way, with updates rolling out over the coming weeks.&nbsp;
Built on the same foundation as PlayStation Spectral Super Resolution (PSSR) on PS5 Pro, QSSR can deliver sharper details, cleaner edges, and more stable images than traditional upscalers. And because it shares its interface with PSSR, it&#8217;s a natural fit for games that already support PSSR.&nbsp;
